.TH BLOT 1
.SH NAME
blot \- device contexts, brushes and blots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/blot
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Blot
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Blot.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Two off-screen device contexts.  The small one is a monochrome brush \- a
filled circle with a diagonal through it \- and setting it as the pen
makes a circle stamp the brush at each plotted point instead of a pixel,
which is what turns the big ring into a chain.  Clearing the brush puts
the pen back to a plain thick line.  The large context is then blotted
across the window in steps of four, and at the end the brush itself is
turned into a sprite and drawn, a device context and a sprite being two
views of the same pixels.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit, once the blot has finished
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/blot.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
